id: pm-vcs-erasureprooftransport
title: Carry physical-erasure verification evidence across transports
description: "Logical erasure denials carry tombstone IDs and payload digests but not the new local byte-window verification evidence. A legacy/imported denial with missing canonical bytes must refuse a fresh physical-erasure certificate until verified source evidence is supplied. Add capability-negotiated transport and validation of fingerprints without changing existing tombstone identities or transporting erased bytes. This is a follow-up to pm-vcs-phase6packs, whose local scanner and resume path already fail closed."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T14:52:31.224Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T14:52:34.681Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A metadata-only clone can obtain and validate source byte-proof metadata without payload bytes; corrupt or foreign evidence refuses; existing denial identities and logical policy remain compatible; file and HTTP transports work outside Git.
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
